aafedfa4698eca8b07b1079"}]},{"sha":"180c357a17c69db79aafedfa4698eca8b07b1079","node_id":"C_kwDOS1J6QtoAKDE4MGMzNTdhMTdjNjlkYjc5YWFmZWRmYTQ2OThlY2E4YjA3YjEwNzk","commit":{"author":{"name":"jy7lsna","email":"jyolsnajoemon@gmail.com","date":"2026-07-08T10:07:02Z"},"committer":{"name":"Statewave","email":"145447586+smaramwbc@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-08T10:10:58Z"},"message":"Configurable domain tools, tests, and docs\n\nMake the multi-agent-memory demo adaptable to any domain instead of the\nhardcoded market-intel scenario:\n- SUBJECT_ID, SYNTHESIS_SYSTEM_PROMPT, and DEMO_SEED_BLOOMBERG_STRIPE are\n  now environment-configurable; agents are discovered dynamically from the\n  sources/ directory.\n- Add a lifespan connectivity probe and a demo-seed reachability path.\n- Add unit tests (candidate building + memory diff) and run them in CI.\n- Add statewave_tools.py — a copy-paste remember()/compile()/recall()\n  helper, and a README \"npx (fastest)\" quickstart.\n\nReconciled onto the official SDK migration: server.py and statewave_tools.py\nuse AsyncStatewaveClient / StatewaveClient and StatewaveConnectionError\ninstead of raw httpx; no httpx dependency remains.","tree":{"sha":"b1bf9af6b158125b0b52c52b65749f6ee4fa24e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smaramwbc/statewave-multi-agent-memory/git/trees/b1bf9af6b158125b0b52c52b65749f6ee4fa24e8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smaramwbc/statewave-multi-agent-memory/git/commits/180c357a17c69db79aafedfa4698eca8b07b1079","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smaramwbc/statewave-multi-agent-memory/commits/180c357a17c69db79aafedfa4698eca8b07b1079","html_url":"https://github.com/smaramwbc/statewave-multi-agent-memory/commit/180c357a17c69db79aafedfa4698eca8b07b1079","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smaramwbc/statewave-multi-agent-memory/commits/180c357a17c69db79aafedfa4698eca8b